    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλῠ-γόνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>generating females</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Steril.</u>
				230
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ γυναῖκες καὶ ἄνδρες . . θ. εἰσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					585b13
				</span></i>
			; of animals, ib.<i><span class="en">
				573b32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GA</u>
				766b32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλυγόνον, τό</span>, a plant supposed <i>to promote the generation
				of females, dog-mercury, Mercurialis perennis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.18.5
			</span></i>; <i>a variety of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύλλον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.125
			</span></i>;= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λινόζωστις θήλεια</span>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.189
			</span></i>.</div>
